{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>When you besiege a city.</b> They do not besiege a Canaanite city less than three days before the Sabbath, and if they have surrounded it and the Sabbath happens to fall, the Sabbath does not interrupt its warfare. This is one of the three things that Shammai the Elder said: they do not launch the ship into the great sea except three days before the Sabbath. In what case? In a distant journey; but in a nearby journey they may launch it. And this applies to those on optional errands, but for those on a religious errand it is a religious duty for them to set out on whatever day they wish." "<b>You shall not destroy its tree.</b> The one adjacent to it." "<b>For from it you shall eat.</b> After you conquer it." "<b>For the human is a tree of the field.</b> Rashi explained: here כי serves in the sense of 'perhaps,' etc. And with wonder: perhaps you think that the tree of the field's custom and practice is to enter inside the siege because of you, like a human, and you have permission to cut it down, and it would suffer the afflictions of hunger and thirst like the people of the city whom the soldiers starve in a siege — since this is not so, why would you destroy it?"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:53:35.390215520Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}